Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["InfraEchoFunction", "ObjectName",
 CellID->1224892054,ExpressionUUID->"8393d601-4014-44ba-afc9-60862df940ec"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"4f96fc81-b57d-4e50-93e9-41285006168e"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["InfraEchoFunction"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraCausality/ref/InfraEchoFunction", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraCausality Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["b", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d468337e-f55e-4f09-aab3-ea0b7b459134"],
 "\[LineSeparator]",
 "is the echo relation of the observer ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 " via the observer ",
 StyleBox["b", "TI"],
 ": each tick of ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 " goes to the ticks of ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 " that receive the light returned from ",
 StyleBox["b", "TI"],
 ". Its members are the echo functions, the compositions of a message \
function from ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 " to ",
 StyleBox["b", "TI"],
 " with a message function from ",
 StyleBox["b", "TI"],
 " back to ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 ".",
 "\n"
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"109bdaf5-c1a7-47e5-acaa-2d276cad32db"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Definition: with the message relations ",
 StyleBox["M", "TI"],
 "ab from ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 " to ",
 StyleBox["b", "TI"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["M", "TI"],
 "ba from ",
 StyleBox["b", "TI"],
 " to ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 " of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraMessageFunction"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraCausality/ref/InfraMessageFunction", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraCausality Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "4c6d23e1-4ecb-49a4-af4c-74b80974cbf8"],
 ", the echo relation sends a tick ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 " of ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 " to Echo(",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ") = \[Union] ",
 StyleBox["M", "TI"],
 "ba(",
 StyleBox["w", "TI"],
 ") over ",
 StyleBox["w", "TI"],
 " \[Element] ",
 StyleBox["M", "TI"],
 "ab(",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 "), the ticks of ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 " lit by the return signals. An echo function is a composition ",
 StyleBox["t", "TI"],
 " \[SmallCircle] ",
 StyleBox["s", "TI"],
 " of a message function ",
 StyleBox["s", "TI"],
 " from ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 " to ",
 StyleBox["b", "TI"],
 " and a message function ",
 StyleBox["t", "TI"],
 " from ",
 StyleBox["b", "TI"],
 " to ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 ", both order-preserving selections (EPS axiom D1), defined on the ticks ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 " of ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 " whose signal returns, that is ",
 StyleBox["s", "TI"],
 "(",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ") has a message back. Two pairs (",
 StyleBox["s", "TI"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["t", "TI"],
 ") can give the same echo function, and the members are the distinct \
composites."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"e8237e33-07b4-4ba8-96e7-e896b8410ee4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Every echo function preserves the order of ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 ", but not every order-preserving map into the echo relation is an echo \
function: a map with admissible images may factor only through a selection \
that reverses the order of two message images. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraEchoFunctionQ"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraCausality/ref/InfraEchoFunctionQ", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraCausality Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "70b5206e-f5b6-49b6-834c-4639995844cf"],
 " decides membership exactly and without enumeration: the map must be \
order-preserving with its domain among the ticks that have a message, and the \
layered selection DAG of ",
 StyleBox["M", "TI"],
 "ab, restricted to the images ",
 StyleBox["w", "TI"],
 " of a tick ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 " with ",
 StyleBox["f", "TI"],
 "(",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ") \[Element] ",
 StyleBox["M", "TI"],
 "ba(",
 StyleBox["w", "TI"],
 ") (or with ",
 StyleBox["M", "TI"],
 "ba(",
 StyleBox["w", "TI"],
 ") empty when ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 " is outside the domain of ",
 StyleBox["f", "TI"],
 "), with an edge between equal images of consecutive ticks kept only when ",
 StyleBox["f", "TI"],
 " takes the same value on both, must have a path from the first tick to the \
last. A path is a selection ",
 StyleBox["s", "TI"],
 ", and ",
 StyleBox["t", "TI"],
 " is read off it as ",
 StyleBox["t", "TI"],
 "(",
 StyleBox["s", "TI"],
 "(",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ")) = ",
 StyleBox["f", "TI"],
 "(",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 "); ",
 StyleBox["t", "TI"],
 " is order-preserving because ",
 StyleBox["f", "TI"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["s", "TI"],
 " are, and it extends to the ticks of ",
 StyleBox["b", "TI"],
 " that ",
 StyleBox["s", "TI"],
 " misses because each message image is an initial segment of the future of \
its tick on ",
 StyleBox["b", "TI"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"9ac09179-c476-4741-9925-372d69b52b9f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The echo is the round trip of radar: the observer ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 " sends a signal at tick ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ", it is reflected at ",
 StyleBox["b", "TI"],
 ", and it comes back at a later tick. In Minkowski space the echo is a \
single event, and the emission and reception times give the radar time and \
distance of the reflection event. On a graph the echo of a tick can be \
several ticks, or none when the signal misses ",
 StyleBox["b", "TI"],
 " or the return misses ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 "; every echo lies strictly after its tick."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"d720b0a1-77e9-44a6-884f-3b64e7da54db"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The head holds its two observers and computes nothing. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraMeasurement"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraMeasurement", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "e48d9ae1-714e-4012-b10f-fd890bd6741e"],
 " reads it on a graph:"
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"efd5d45c-8529-4246-a8e6-a60df84600a6"],

Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "4d26f583-6e7e-46d6-9513-095c0fd237dd"], Cell["Property", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"9d42a104-01eb-47f1-ae3a-86b560339679"],
     Cell["Value", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"e9ac72c7-c604-4400-b435-6fc9d36f599c"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "ec0c42df-7da3-4ae3-ad0d-ae8185bad01b"], Cell[TextData[Cell[
    BoxData["\"\<Relation\>\""], "InlineFormula",
     FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
     "7ec91187-65c5-4db4-8603-f24ea386cdd9"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "bc50c123-33de-4447-8323-94828f034f90"], Cell[TextData[{
     "the association ",
     StyleBox["v", "TI"],
     " \[RightArrow] Echo(",
     StyleBox["v", "TI"],
     ") over every tick of ",
     StyleBox["a", "TI"],
     ", echoes in the order of ",
     StyleBox["a", "TI"]
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"b4389114-657d-4f55-b0c6-2ed1d85103f7"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "3346760b-7c91-4282-a34e-58862c184a0c"], Cell[TextData[Cell[
    BoxData["\"\<Graph\>\""], "InlineFormula",
     FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
     "2f7d27f0-1c87-45f0-91db-98b05760908b"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "f62e4b0f-064b-4a21-addb-50a701b7b4fe"], Cell[TextData[{
     "the directed graph ",
     StyleBox["v", "TI"],
     " \[RightArrow] ",
     StyleBox["u", "TI"],
     " of the relation, on the ticks of ",
     StyleBox["a", "TI"]
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"ba6885ed-cbe4-426f-9049-1cf78ecf0ca9"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "b945da58-36f1-425e-99a7-e01d1cbb1f56"], Cell[TextData[Cell[
    BoxData["\"\<Cardinality\>\""], "InlineFormula",
     FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
     "b3772ca2-8a67-4965-b8be-bcce830c0a88"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "6966fa00-6fdb-4eb3-a624-92cde5ec39a0"], Cell["\<\
the number of distinct echo functions, by enumeration of the two sets of \
message functions; at most the product of the two message cardinalities\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"e1d9b781-4799-4024-8fb8-6f7919fa274b"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "d50d269d-d2db-4750-a1e1-3ab6e70e3e10"], Cell[TextData[Cell[
    BoxData["\"\<Faithful\>\""], "InlineFormula",
     FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
     "d83477ee-39ba-4a27-b791-3d04efc0371d"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "c2bc6302-9b4f-4539-9d93-caa93c9e2acd"], Cell[TextData[Cell[BoxData[
    "True"], "InlineFormula",
     FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
     "47ca0c46-7906-462c-ac0a-bbeff6557ca0"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "c7620b5f-9005-475a-b68c-dcfd7dcebef0"]}
  }]], "2ColumnTableMod",ExpressionUUID->"8f986042-935e-46de-a71d-\
fa479d5b7175"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A member is an association from ticks of ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 " to ticks of ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 ". ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraEchoFunctionQ"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraCausality/ref/InfraEchoFunctionQ", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraCausality Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "14a3d1e4-a62a-4160-92bc-4d48abb6e9c9"],
 " decides membership, and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraMemberQ"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraMemberQ", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "170a512e-537e-482b-ae18-a47786634462"],
 " is the same test; the experimental ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["RandomInfraEchoFunction"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraCausality/ref/RandomInfraEchoFunction", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraCausality Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "ffa3193a-682c-4201-acdc-b34cb52a0b89"],
 " draws members or enumerates them. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraSubstrateHighlight"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraSubstrateHighlight", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "cbaefffb-a6c7-4b46-b384-513fe60935b6"],
 " draws the head as the outgoing and returning light rays."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"2a793763-d671-413e-9690-a5445b1de6ba"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Experimental: the EPS defects of the echo relation are the four defects of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraMessageFunction"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraCausality/ref/InfraMessageFunction", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraCausality Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "8ab93060-4e21-48fc-84a0-6cc10fa9935e"],
 " read on the relation ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 " \[RightArrow] Echo(",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 "), on the window of ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 " left by the option ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\"\<Boundary\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "b"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4d444379-77a3-4ba9-a0fc-3bae41c340ab"],
 " (a fourth argument, default 0), with the echoes anywhere on ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 ": ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<DomainDefect\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "74382ff9-90a7-4fbc-b54c-7bd35455c423"],
 " the fraction of window ticks without an echo, ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<FunctionDefect\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e704082d-99c7-4004-8a98-2a5a88e1f5f8"],
 " the mean of max(0, ",
 "|",
 "Echo(",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ")",
 "|",
 " \[Minus] 1) / max(1, ",
 "|",
 "Echo(",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ")",
 "|",
 "), ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<InjectivityDefect\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "fbbec2d9-0b62-4d68-8043-ac1feebc36a6"],
 " 1 \[Minus] \[Nu] / ",
 StyleBox["n", "TI"],
 " with \[Nu] a maximum matching of the relation, and ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<OrderDefect\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "898f1b53-72ce-46bb-9e6f-475fcf5574a6"],
 " the fraction of ordered window pairs ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 " before ",
 StyleBox["w", "TI"],
 " with an echo of ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 " after an echo of ",
 StyleBox["w", "TI"],
 ". In Minkowski space the echo of an inertial observer via another is a \
monotone injection of its clock into itself, and all four vanish."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"75aed6d1-3d70-4461-93d1-767fa8ab266e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<KFactor\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1fef4677-b5a4-4852-9113-e313cdd3215f"],
 " is the square root of the ratio of echo to tick spans of the earliest-echo \
selection: with ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["w", "TI"],
 " the first and last window ticks that have an echo, \[Sqrt]((pos ",
 StyleBox["e", "TI"],
 "(",
 StyleBox["w", "TI"],
 ") \[Minus] pos ",
 StyleBox["e", "TI"],
 "(",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ")) / (pos ",
 StyleBox["w", "TI"],
 " \[Minus] pos ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ")), positions counted on ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 ". In Minkowski space an observer receding at speed ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 " returns the radar signal of another after ",
 StyleBox["k", "TI"],
 "\.b2 times the sending time, with ",
 StyleBox["k", "TI"],
 " = \[Sqrt]((1 + ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ")/(1 \[Minus] ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ")) the Bondi factor, so the square root is the Bondi factor under \
reciprocity, ",
 StyleBox["k", "TI"],
 "ab = ",
 StyleBox["k", "TI"],
 "ba. The reading uses the clock of ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 " alone: on the diamond lattice the resting chain {(",
 StyleBox["m", "TI"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["m", "TI"],
 ")} echoed by the chain {((",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 " + 1)",
 StyleBox["m", "TI"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["pm", "TI"],
 ")} of velocity 1/(2",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 " + 1) reads exactly \[Sqrt]((",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 " + 1)/",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 "), the Bondi factor, although the moving chain's ticks are not its proper \
time. On sprinklings the longest chains between two events wander, so two \
observers with a given endpoint velocity share stretches of their worldlines \
and the reading scatters widely at a few hundred events."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"1c84f37a-f590-4dd2-8e56-7efd40ff69aa"],

Cell["Corresponding notions:", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"adee4b31-3dd3-45f6-9645-938bc36cbb42"],

